title: "Automated Compliance Verification for EU AI Act Article 9: A Three-Layer Neuro-Symbolic Framework"
authors:
  - family-names: "Vahedi Sarrigani"
    given-names: "Hoda"
    affiliation: "Liverpool John Moores University; UrbanChain Ltd"
  - family-names: "Lee"
    given-names: "Gyu Myoung"
    affiliation: "Liverpool John Moores University"
abstract: >-
  A three-layer neuro-symbolic framework for automated verification of EU AI Act
  Article 9 (risk management) compliance evidence for healthcare AI. Layer 1
  extracts the article into a SHACL-validated knowledge graph with a local LLM;
  Layer 2 uses the same LLM to check whether mitigations fit their claimed
  risk-control level and severities fit the described harm; Layer 3 classifies
  each evidence package with a dual-shield graph neural network using noise-aware
  fusion, with confidence-based deferral to human review. Evaluated on a
  reproducible synthetic dataset grounded in ISO 14971 and a public FDA submission.
keywords:
  - "EU AI Act"
  - "regulatory compliance"
  - "neuro-symbolic AI"
  - "knowledge graphs"
  - "SHACL"
  - "graph neural networks"
  - "large language models"
  - "healthcare AI"
